# TeamFlow Governance — Required

Before any coding or file changes, read the repository-root `AGENTS.md` completely and follow it. It is the canonical source of project decisions and engineering rules for both Antigravity and Cursor.

Non-negotiable: do not assume missing requirements, technologies, architecture, package choices, data relationships, permissions, API behavior, or deployment details. Inspect first; distinguish confirmed decisions from repository facts and unknowns; ask the user about unresolved consequential decisions; stop before implementation until they answer and any required plan is approved.

For every meaningful addition or change, explain its purpose, why it is needed, what depends on it, and what would happen if it were removed. Do not install packages, change schemas, modify public APIs, perform destructive operations, or create paid/external cloud resources without the required explanation and approval.

Implement one approved feature at a time. Explain and test the actual behavior; report exact verification results and unresolved issues. If information is missing, ask. Do not guess and do not code.
